# Vercel serves ONLY the Vite frontend. The FastAPI backend runs on Render,
# which clones from Git — so nothing here affects the backend deploy.
#
# Why this file exists: Vercel auto-detects a framework from the repo contents.
# `requirements.txt` listing fastapi, combined with `main.py` defining a
# top-level `app` (main.py is one of Vercel's recognised Python entrypoint
# filenames), makes Vercel pick the FastAPI preset and build the backend on
# Vercel — where it tries to compile scikit-learn from source.
#
# Excluding these also trims the upload (the model alone is ~25 MB).

# Python backend
main.py
requirements.txt
.python-version

# Model, data and notebooks (not needed to build the frontend)
Mental_Health_Model.pkl
ML_Project.ipynb
*.csv

# Test / utility scripts
test_suite.py
capture_remaining.py
